 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL c  J|p=0+ for {+32}S ground state.                                        
 35CL c  1970Ho09: {+32}S(|a,p|g) E=10.975, 11.960, 12.120 MeV alpha beams      
 35CL2c  produced from the Chalk River MP tandem accelerator. Target of a 100   
 35CL3c  |mg/cm{+2} Sb{-2}S{-3} on a 10 |mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Six          
 35CL4c  15.2-cm-long by 12.7-cm-diam NaI(Tl) detectors for detecting |g-rays   
 35CL5c  and an annular silicon surface detector for detecting protons, FWHM=30 
 35CL6c  keV. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g, p|g(|q). Deduced levels, J,         
 35CL7c  branchings, mixing ratios.                                             
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Br33: {+32}S(|a,p|g), E=10 MeV alpha beam from the Chalk River MP  
 35CL2c  tandem accelerator. Targets of 340 |mg/cm{+2} Sb{-2}S{-3} on a gold    
 35CL3c  backing. A 44 cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector inside a split annular NaI(Tl)    
 35CL4c  detector for detecting |g-rays. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced level       
 35CL5c  energy, branching, T{-1/2} using DSAM.                                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Al22: 12-16-MeV |a beams were produced from the 80-cm cyclotron at 
 35CL2c  cyclotron at the Research Institute for Physics in Stockholm and the   
 35CL3c  Uppsala tandem accelerator. Targets were prepared by depositing        
 35CL4c  pulverized sulphur enriched to 99.9% in {+32}S on lead backings. |g    
 35CL5c  rays were detected using an Ortec 60-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector with       
 35CL6c  FWHM=2.2 keV at 1333 keV and an additional Canberra 60-cm{+3} Ge(Li)   
 35CL7c  detector for coincidence measurements. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,   
 35CL8c  |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, branching ratios, and mixing ratios.        
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1969In04: {+32}S(|a,p|g) E=6-8 MeV alpha beam produced from the Chalk  
 35CL2c  River MP tandem accelerator. A thick target (270 |mg/cm{+2}) of natural
 35CL3c  sulfur on a tantalum backing and a thin target (50 |mg/cm{+2} of       
 35CL4c  Sb{-2}S{-3} on a gold backing. Two Ge(Li) detectors of 15 and 40 cm{+3}
 35CL5c  for detecting |g-rays. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, branchings,  
 35CL6c  half-lives using the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM) and Recoil
 35CL7c  Distance Method (RDM).                                                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1970In01: a 10-MeV |a beam was produced at the Chalk River Nuclear     
 35CL2c  Laboratories. Targets were 340-|mg/cm{+2} Sb{-2}S{-3} on a gold        
 35CL3c  backing. |g rays were detected using a 44-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector inside
 35CL4c  a split annular NaI(Tl) detector. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced levels, J,
 35CL5c  |p, branching ratios, the lifetime using the Doppler Shift Attenuation 
 35CL6c  Method (DSAM) for a level at 3942 keV.                                 
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973Br26: a 11.2-MeV |a beam was produced from the Legnaro (Padova) Van
 35CL2c  de Graaff generator. Targets were natural CdS. |g rays were detected   
 35CL3c  using a Ge(Li) detector. Deduced the lifetime using the Recoil Distance
 35CL4c  Method (RDM) for a level at 3163 keV.                                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1973An01: 5.5- and 8.6-MeV |a beams of 100-200 nA were produced from   
 35CL2c  the Oxford Vertical Van de Graaff (Injector) or the Oxford E(n) Tandem.
 35CL3c  Targets were natural sulphur in AgS. |g rays were detected using a     
 35CL4c  Ge(Li) detector at 0|'. Measured E|g, I|g. Deduced lifetimes using the 
 35CL5c  Recoil Distance Method (RDM) for a level at 3163 keV.                  
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1974Lo17: 11.0, 12.0 and 14.7-MeV |a beams were produced from the      
 35CL2c  Oliver Lodge Laboratory at the University of Liverpool. Targets were   
 35CL3c  natural sulphur in CdS. Protons were detected using an annular |DE-E   
 35CL4c  telescope with FWHM=80 keV. |g rays were detected using five 5 in by 6 
 35CL5c  in NaI(Tl) and a Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g, p|g(|q), |g-ray   
 35CL6c  linear polarization. Deduced levels, J, |p, branching ratios, mixing   
 35CL7c  ratios, and lifetimes using DSAM and RDM for 3 levels at 4348, 5408,   
 35CL8c  and 6088 keV.                                                          
